WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.335
-Our next guest is a talente
actor you know from his work

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.270 size:88% position:44%
on the "Captain America"
and "Avengers" movies.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.605 line:92%
He returns as Bucky Barnes

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier,"

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is available
exclusively on Disney Plus

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
with new episodes
releasing on Fridays.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.513 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're alone.
You're 100 years old.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have no history,
no family --

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.220 line:92%
-Are you lashing out at me, Doc?

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because that's really
unprofessional.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I mean,
when did that start?

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
When'd you start yelling
at your clients?

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, the notebook. That's great
[ Sighs ]

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right. Give me a break
I'm trying. Okay?

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:34.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
This isn't -- [ Sighs ]
This is new for me.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.070 size:81% position:41%
I didn't have a moment
to deal with anything.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know?

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.741 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I had a little...calm.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
In Wakanda.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:47.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
And other than that, I jus
went from one fight to another

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for 90 years.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the sho
Sebastian Stan.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks for being here,
Sebastian.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, man,
thank you for having me.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like
there were two things

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were all very desperate for
over the last year --

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.730 line:92%
vaccines and new Marvel content.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it feels like
they're dovetailing together

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.101 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
very nicely.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:08.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Yes.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:12.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
Perfect timing for both of us,
I guess.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:12.839 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So, I have to ask,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.842
when you and your co-star
Anthony Mackie were --

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.711
this was first presented to you,
was it surprising?

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you know
this project was coming?

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, we didn't.
We just both knew

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:26.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were going to stick aroun
in some capacity.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, because we were aliv
at the end of "Endgame."

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:34.861
But, then, we had both gotte
called in, unbeknownst to us

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.696 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you know, for a meeting.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
we had separate meetings,

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:42.335 size:84% position:42%
but then I ran into him
at this hotel in L.A.,

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn't know
he was in L.A.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he, like,
looked at me funny,

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:49.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I looked at him funny,
and we sort of started

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
to kind of
piece the puzzle together

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe we were there
for the same reason, you know?

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the puzzles
anybody in show business

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
has had to piece together
this year

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
is how to shoot during COVID
obviously.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:01.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You were --

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:05.125
In the middle of it, you wer
going to Prague last March

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very difficult
with Anthony

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.061 line:92%
because he's a close talker.

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:11.764
So, you know, the aspect
of social distance for him

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:12.932 size:78% position:39% line:92%
is a difficult thing.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:13.900 line:92%
But, yeah, we were in Prague

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.936
-It's like a normal 6 feet, bu
it's like an Anthony 12 feet

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:20.373
Is that what you're saying
-[ Laughs ] Yeah, exactly.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:24.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you flew to Prague.
This was, I guess, last year

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.812 line:92%
Before everything shut down.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:28.014 line:92%
And I will say I tip my cap.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:30.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
Early on, you were
taking this very serious.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's you on an airplane.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.220 line:92%
Yeah, well, thank God Fox News

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
reported on it at the time
you know?

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:41.594
But we did because, you know
we didn't know what to expect.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had my best friend
with me,

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's a worse hypochondria
than I was.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we just kept piling things
on and going --

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, where do we stop
with this thing?

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
it was our first --

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.340 line:92%
my first picture of this hashtag

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were trying out
called #BuckyTakesEurope,

00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which, of course,
led to only three posts

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:04.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a birthday that happened
a few days later.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.686 line:92%
And then we were sent back

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard you were
actually celebrating

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.256 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Bucky's 106th birthday

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:14.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you found out
that everything was shut down.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.028 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep. Yeah.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:18.398
We were -- We decided to fin
one of the most authentic,

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:23.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, places in Prague
to go and have dinner,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.772 line:92%
and it was a crowded place

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:28.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we thought
it was funny at the time,

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:32.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it led to me
meeting about 35 waiters

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
and hugging them
and taking selfies with them

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, 10 minutes later
we got a call.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were supposed to
get on a plane.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:44.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I felt really good
about how I spent that night..

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.159 size:84% position:42% line:92%
more at risk than ever.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.361 size:75% position:38%
-Now, I have to ask,
you know, obviously,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.629 line:92%
you're not Bucky's age yet

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you have been playing
this character for 10 years.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it harder --
Do you find the recovery harde

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the intense
action sequences

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they put
your character through?

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Well, it's usually
by the end of the press tour

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:06.112 size:81% position:41%
so you can get closer
and closer to the age.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But, yeah.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I think we both
take quite a lot of Advil,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:13.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, and there's --
and definitely some ice packs.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.988 line:92%
But, you know, it's just -

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:17.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got to get Anthony
off the ground a lot more.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:20.326
-[ Laughs ] That's right.
Very nice how I feel like

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have a lot of empathy
for Anthony.

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:25.365
It's really sweet that you'r
sharing that with us today

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I do, you know,
but it's sort of something

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.002 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you have to live with.

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:32.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like --
You know, it's like a diseas

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:35.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're just gonna
have to live with.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:36.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we --
I think, look, you know,

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:40.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
we kind of know each other wel
and we have a good rapport

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
and somehow they decided
to give us a show,

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.421
you know, to have more,
so it's been a privilege.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.289 line:92%
-You came back from Prague

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
when everything got shut dow
in New York City.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know that you had
lived here before.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:55.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were an actor
here in New York City.

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:59.065
What was it like for you
last spring being in a cit

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.700 line:92%
that obviously we all know

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
is much more vibrant
than it was then?

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.004 line:92%
-Well, it was really strange

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.840
I mean, because, you know,
we didn't really know what -

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.042 line:92%
at the time what to expect

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so everything
felt out of place.

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, I think
the emptiness of the streets

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:19.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I went full on like
"The Aviator" DiCaprio OCD

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I was taking
my clothes off in my hallway

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
and running them
to the washing machine

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:29.562
and then washing every littl
thing, you know, in the sink

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.430 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And it was really weird.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.500
But I had this old lady
across the street from me

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.035 line:92%
who every night at 7:00 p.m.

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
would come out
and just blast Frank Sinatra

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, and then,
everybody else would come ou

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.241 line:92%
and just sort of join in.

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:45.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that -- Moments like tha
just feel kind of that --

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.813 size:81% position:41% line:92%
They surpass all time.

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:49.415 size:78% position:39%
-I always like asking
anybody who was young

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
living in New York,
especially actors,

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:55.121
what their first -- their
early apartments were like

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:59.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you have any doozies
back in your day?

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:02.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was --
I'll say exactly where it was.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:05.465 line:92%
It was at 323 West 42nd Street

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
right across
from Port Authority.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, great area. Great area.
Beautiful.

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:12.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
But we were in Times Square.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.540 line:92%
So, you know, we felt lucky.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:18.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How many roommates
were you rocking back then

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, well, I had
one official roommate

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.483 line:92%
that paid the rent with me

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:26.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we had all of our
Rutgers friends kind of, like,

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
just hop off the bus,
cross the street,

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then crash with us,
you know?

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.991 line:92%
But it was -- I don't know

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:35.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everything about that
was romantic at the time.

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:39.265
That's what we said to ourselves
until you walked outside.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:43.069
-Yeah. And you would also,
I'm sure, say it to girls.

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:44.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You want to see
something romantic?

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:47.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've never seen romance
until you've seen

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.775 line:92%
the Port Authority at night.

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:50.576 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Oh, yes. Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:52.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
That will definitely
shake things up.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:55.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like the one neighborhoo
they just haven't tried

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:56.716 size:81% position:41% line:92%
giving a cute name to.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:58.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're like, "No."

00:06:58.117 --> 00:07:00.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We've got a one-bedroom
in Port Thor."

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
It's always what it is.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.024 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But in a way, you know,

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was something
grounding about it.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:09.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like --
You walk out in New York City.

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:10.229 line:92%
You know, you're always --

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
Life greets you,
and it kind of puts you on a -

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
reminds you
of the right things I guess.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think
you're right about that.

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.705
And congrats on the show.
It's so exciting to watch.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thanks so much
for being here.

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:22.508 line:92%
-Thank you. Thank you, man

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolutely. Thanks so much
I'll see you.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:26.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-New episodes of "The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier"

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:30.983
are available on Fridays
